{
  "id": "how-task-run-failures-are-recorded",
  "title": "How task run failures are recorded",
  "kind": "location",
  "answers": [
    "Where are task run failures recorded?",
    "How is error_type derived for a failed run?",
    "How is error message truncated for telemetry?"
  ],
  "body": "- Workflow: `workflow.py:ProcessTaskWorkflow._update_task_run_status(status, error_message, error_type, timed_out_inactivity, ...)` calls the update_task_run_status activity; `workflow.py:_failure_error_type` maps temporal TimeoutType (lowercased name), string cause type, else exception class name.\n- Model: `models.py:TaskRun.mark_failed`; facade `fail_task_run` and `claim_and_fail_stale_run` are janitor/reaper paths.\n- Telemetry: `backend/error_telemetry.py:truncate_error_message` keeps the tail (500 chars) since root cause is at the end of agent output.",
